.DS_Store
node_modules
/build
/.svelte-kit
/package
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
vite.config.js.timestamp-*
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*

# OpenSubtitles application key used during development. Release builds bake one
# in at compile time and can override it through the same signed channel as
# latest.json.
src-tauri/.opensubtitles-key

# Binary SDKs — large, downloaded by scripts/fetch-libs.ps1
src-tauri/lib/*.dll
src-tauri/lib/*.so
src-tauri/lib/*.dylib
src-tauri/ffmpeg/
src-tauri/tools/

# Generated linking directory for ffmpeg on macOS (scripts/bundle-macos-libs.sh)
src-tauri/ffmpeg-macos/

# Fixture for the sidecar smoke tests (see README, "Building")
/test.mp4

# Session handoff between machines: carries LAN details and personal file
# paths, so it must never be committed. Transfer it out of band, like a note in
# a password manager.
#
# The pattern itself was missing until now — the comment was here and the line
# it describes was not, so the one file the repository rules say must never be
# committed was not in fact ignored.
HANDOFF.md

# `go build ./...` inside services/relay writes the binary next to its source.
server/relay
services/relay/relay

# The compiled service binaries from `go build`, which land in the repo root.
tmdb
relay
